 et/29788696/d9da678f-d6f7-41c9-914e-a6ed7af9a724.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:San Francisco AIDS Foundation\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/el-grupo-de-apoyo-latino-ticket
 s
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Her Story\, History\, Their Story\, Whose Story? Facts and Fiction
 s in Historical Queer Books
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17837544@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:LOCATION\n\nGLBT Historical Society Museum\n\n4127 18th Street
 \n\nSan Francisco\, CA 94114\n\nADMISSION\n\n$10\; Free for GLBT Historica
 l Society Members\n\nRSVP and reserve tickets here\n\nThe GLBT Historical 
 Society in partnership with the Bay Area Reporter and Litquake present a p
 anel discussion as part of the 2026 Litquake festival!\n\nWhat are the rul
 es of engagement when telling historical tales about the lives of LGBTQ ch
 aracters? Authors and scholars compare notes on their fictional and nonfic
 tion works that resonate realistically\, and even those that are completel
 y fantastical yet set in the real world’s past. Featuring authors Mark A
 bramson\, Lucy Jane Bledsoe\, Joey Cain\, and Katie Gilmartin. Moderated b
 y Bay Area Reporter arts editor and author Jim Provenzano.\n\nMODERATOR: J
 im Provenzano (he/him) is the author of seven novels\, including the Lambd
 a Literary Award winner Every Time I Think of You\, and its sequel Message
  of Love (a Lambda finalist)\, his debut novel PINS and its award-winning 
 commissioned stage adaptation. Other works include four audiobook adaptati
 ons\, a short story collection and a novella. The guest-curator of Sportin
 g Life\, the world’s first gay athletics exhibit at the GLBT Historical 
 Society Museum\, he also wrote the syndicated Sports Complex column for te
 n years. A journalist\, editor and photographer in LGBTQ media for more th
 an three decades\, he lives in San Francisco\, and is the Arts Editor of t
 he Bay Area Reporter. https://www.jimprovenzano.com/\n\nMark Abramson (...
 \n\n$10\n\nTickets: https://herstory_history_litquake.eventbrite.com\nDeta
 ils: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/her-story-history-their-story-
 whose-story-facts-and-fictions-in-historical-queer-books-tickets\nSource: 
 DoTheBay
GEO:37.7608609;-122.4356584
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34423966/2460d8dc-72a4-40ea-bab7-d359d6a6d86e.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:GLBT History Museum\, 4127 18th St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/her-story-history-their-story-w
 hose-story-facts-and-fictions-in-historical-queer-books-tickets
END:VEVENT
